Z||000008||87ECO5||03-13-2001||07:47 AM||||Hmmmm ... it's unlike the IndiOhio folks to not chime in right about now.  We must be getting burned out.     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Let's see ... the main two have already been mentioned:  C.O.F.E.'s "Ohio Fiero Meet" on June 23rd and the "Vintage Sports Car Races at Mid-Ohio" on June 24th.  Distance between the two is small (less than 50 miles).  C.O.F.E.'s event is in Wooster, Mid-Ohio is in Lexington.<P>2M4 Dale has mentioned having his 2nd annual Fiero picnic this August at his home.  Last year, he had about a dozen Fieros show up.  We ate TONS of food, swam in his pool, drove to the old Mansfield prison for a Fiero photo shoot, sang songs around a huge bonfire, and slept in tents in his backyard (he lives out in the middle of nowhere!).  It was a blast!  I hope he doesn't mind me advertising it.<P>Dale also supports the Ashland-Mansfield Fiero club.  About this time last year, we had our "grand opening" meeting at Mohican State Park.  About 15 Fieros showed up.  I think we'll be doing that again.  It too was a blast!<P>I started an IndiOhio club last year.  It consists of several PFF members:  2M4 Dale, BOILERMAKER, BENGAL4, ChadMan, fiero56, Monkeyman, tgowens, william_thorniii, and myself.  We don't really have "official" shows but, several of us get together so often, it ends up being a show of sorts.<P>... somebody turn that babbling switch off for me, OK!?     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by 87ECO5 (edited 03-13-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||rogergarrison||03-13-2001||11:12 AM||||Anytime any of you get together, send me a Email. Im always looking for an excuse and place to go when the suns shining. Ill take off to nowhere around 10am and not come back till evening just to go for lunch somewhere. Hate the freeways, rather take back ways.||||reg||1
